<title>USA: AOL to take charges.</title>
<headline>AOL to take charges.</headline>
<dateline>DULLES, Va. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>America Online Inc said it immediately will begin expensing all marketing and subscriber acquistion costs as they are incurred, rather than deferring the costs and amortizing them over time as it did previously.</p>
<p>The company said it will take a charge as of September 30, 1996 of about $385 million, representing the balance of deferred subscriber acquisition costs as of that date.</p>
<p>In addition, AOL plans to take a one-time charge in the December 1996 quarter of up to $75 million, representing costs it expects to incur as it reorganizes the company.</p>
<p>AOL had been criticized for its old accounting method.</p>
</text>
